{"seq":16,"trial_id":"waterfall-frontier-2026-11/hermes-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T04:15:15.039Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"67e3c5fe0c5eb5ec350cf068a713c980b1a27dcd00eba3d910b85e31829cf4a3","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DWATERF0001","text":"Here's what I found. Moss's notes mention two Quarrendon Freight Lines tickets:\n\n1. #PD-4492, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell logged it on 4 Oct 2025: the gatehouse kiosk at the Eau Claire yard (Dock Doors 14-18) wasn't sending SMS bay assignments to drivers on the 04:00 shift. Support patched it at 19:30 that day, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct shift got through cleanly. There was a follow-up to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n2. #4419, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Also from Thea: the gatehouse barcode scanners couldn't read trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 for scanner firmware testing. That note has no date.\n\nSome things to watch:\n- 4492 and 4419 look alike, and both involve Door 14, but the notes describe two separate issues (SMS vs. scanners). Worth checking against the ticket system before they go in the weekly notes.\n- The 9/14 pipeline digest and the 2026-03-23 renewal check-in both mention QFL but don't give a ticket number.\n- I left out #4409, #4412 and FR-882 from Moss's Central handoff digest. Those are Marrow tickets, not QFL. Marcus's note on \"Quarendon Freightways\" (one r) is about a different company that isn't our customer, and it has no tickets anyway.\n- Moss's Central cheat sheet has nothing on QFL."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DWATERF0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
{"seq":17,"trial_id":"waterfall-frontier-2026-11/hermes-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T04:15:21.988Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"210669e591812c9eebadcd57e97e69abc7129d1cf7a9215b4440ef13e463d6f4","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DWATERF0001","text":"I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers in Moss's notes and sent you the list in our DM.\n\n1. #PD-4492, from Moss's \"Sunday prep for Ruth\" digest dated 5 Oct 2025. Thea Ramaswell logged it on 4 Oct 2025: the gatehouse kiosk at the Eau Claire yard wasn't texting drivers their bay assignments at Dock Doors 14–18 on the 04:00 shift. Support patched it that evening, and Thea confirmed the next morning's shift got through without problems.\n2. #4419, from Moss's undated \"North cheat sheet.\" Also from Thea: the gatehouse barcode scanners couldn't read trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 support for scanner firmware testing.\n\nPoints I flagged in the DM:\n- The two numbers look alike and both involve Door 14, but the notes describe two separate problems: missing texts and failing scanners. It's worth checking both against the ticket system before they go in the weekly notes.\n- Two more Moss notes mention QFL but give no ticket number: the 14 Sep 2025 pipeline digest and the 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in.\n- I left out #4409, #4412 and FR-882 because they belong to a Central team account (Marrow), not QFL. I also left out Marcus's note on \"Quarendon Freightways\" (one r), a different company that isn't a customer.\n\nI only looked at Moss's notes in the shared files, plus the two company-wide channels, which were empty."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DWATERF0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
